## Tests

```powershell
dotnet test .\Palace.Tests\Palace.Tests.csproj
.\BuildAndRun.ps1 . --arch x64
# after launch, with the packaged PID:
.\ui-tests.ps1 -AppPid <pid>
```

`Palace.Tests` covers `PalaceDb` async gating (`PalaceDbAsyncTests`: work runs off the caller's sync context and resumes on it, single-connection serialization, exception propagation, cancellation; compiles `Data/PalaceDb.cs` + `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` into the test project), `ErrorReporter` / `ErrorLog` / `ErrorThrottle` (cancellation is not an error, fatal vs reportable, user message truncation, RunAsync notify/log, unhandled throttle), `LoadGate` (dispose clears after sync/async load failure), `CloudFile.IsOnlineOnly` attribute flags (Recall / Pinned / hydrated `ReparsePoint`+`Offline` / Dropbox `SparseFile`+`ReparsePoint` / stamped `FILE_ATTRIBUTE_OFFLINE`), `CloudFile.IsCloudBacked`, `CloudFile.IsCloudBackedFolder`, `ScanContent` (scan must not read or thumb placeholders), `ScanFastPath` (unchanged size + time + current IndexVersion skips re-hash; any change, orphan, online-only, stub hash or missing size takes the full path; progress throttle; `IndexVersion` column), `ScanNotice` / `ScanWalk` (scan notice for unsupported formats by extension, undecodable / failed files with capped examples, inaccessible folders; walk matches `EnumerateFiles` but skips an unreadable folder instead of throwing, and the scan then does not orphan), `CloudFile.Exists` / `FilterLocalPaths`, `ImageDimensions` refusing online-only paths, `HashService` local hash + cloud stub, `GalleryMedia` provider-thumb / placeholder-tile / `ShowCloudBadge` / `StampIsCloudBacked` / `SourceFolderIsCloud` / kind badges (`ShowVideoBadge` / `ShowGifBadge` / `ShowHdrBadge`, skip headers; overlay `IcnGalleryOverlayHdr` / `IcnGalleryWindowHdr`; `HdrBadgeIconDip` 24 + `HdrBadgeLabel` on Accent because Fluent `Hdr` Regular has no Size16 and Secondary is invisible on tiles; `CatalogHdrFromHeader` keeps existing `IsHdr` when the original cannot be read) / mosaic thumbs skip online-only / full-line folder-header aspect (`FolderHeaderAspect` 32:1, not a 240 DIP mid-row slot) / AVIF uses shell thumb never WIC-open